  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two very long parallel plates, X and Y, have equal and opposite charges. The potential on X is V<sub>X</sub> and that on Y is V<sub>Y</sub> where V<sub>X</sub><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"&gt;\"></span>V<sub>Y</sub> . A point particle of positive charge q and mass m is held at rest midway between the plates.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The particle is then released. Which plate will the particle move toward and what kinetic energy does it have when it reaches the plate?</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p>\n<p>[1]</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Option A is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"B\">Option B is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"C\">Option C is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"D\">Option D is shown in the figure above.</li></ol>"
  },
